/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (  The railway network has a high level of fixed costs and is, therefore, often used as an example of a natural monopoly. In economic theory a natural monopoly often leads to a market which is best controlled by one firm. For many years, railway services in the UK were provided by British Rail \(BR\). BR was a nationalised company owned and run by the government and it had a monopoly on the provision of passenger rail services.  )
/E (  The railway network has a high level of fixed costs and is, therefore, often used as an example of a natural monopoly. In economic theory a natural monopoly often leads to a market which is best controlled by one firm. For many years, railway services in the UK were provided by British Rail \(BR\). BR was a nationalised company owned and run by the government and it had a monopoly on the provision of passenger rail services.  )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
