2424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Uganda, with a population of 42m, has one of the youngest populations on average in the world, with 7 out of 10 people under the age of 25. Incomes in the country have increased by 26% in the last two years. The service sector has grown from 32% of the economy in 1990 to 55% in 2018, with a 15% expansion in the last two years. Today, it is estimated that 44% of Ugandans use the Internet, 70% have a mobile phone and 6% use social media. The growing demand for energy in Uganda is clear. Nevertheless, away from large cities, many individuals still operate in a barter economy. Rural agriculture based areas are still very common. However, their contribution to GDP is now only 24% of the total, down from 56% in 1990; a further reflection of the developing nature of the economy.)
/E (Uganda, with a population of 42m, has one of the youngest populations on average in the world, with 7 out of 10 people under the age of 25. Incomes in the country have increased by 26% in the last two years. The service sector has grown from 32% of the economy in 1990 to 55% in 2018, with a 15% expansion in the last two years. Today, it is estimated that 44% of Ugandans use the Internet, 70% have a mobile phone and 6% use social media. The growing demand for energy in Uganda is clear. Nevertheless, away from large cities, many individuals still operate in a barter economy. Rural agriculture based areas are still very common. However, their contribution to GDP is now only 24% of the total, down from 56% in 1990; a further reflection of the developing nature of the economy.)
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
