2441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (If Shell hopes to gain a control in the market it will need to compete against a former rival. The French firm, Engie, has taken the most decisive step into Africa's home solar market, with the acquisition of Ugandan-based Fenix International. Fenix supplies power to around 250 000 homes in Uganda, through the solar kits it sells in partnership with a mobile network provider.)
/E (If Shell hopes to gain a control in the market it will need to compete against a former rival. The French firm, Engie, has taken the most decisive step into Africa's home solar market, with the acquisition of Ugandan-based Fenix International. Fenix supplies power to around 250 000 homes in Uganda, through the solar kits it sells in partnership with a mobile network provider.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
2442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The popularity of the Fenix home energy system means that the company is growing. It plans to 40expand into other countries, to reach millions more people. "We intend to be in multiple markets)
/E (The popularity of the Fenix home energy system means that the company is growing. It plans to 40expand into other countries, to reach millions more people. "We intend to be in multiple markets)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (across eastern, southern and western Africa," said Chief Executive, Lyndsay Handler. "It's still amazing to me that so many people in Uganda do not have access to power. We provide a decentralised, affordable home system that can completely transform lives. An opportunity to rethink the way that we can achieve universal access to energy," she said.)
/E (across eastern, southern and western Africa," said Chief Executive, Lyndsay Handler. "It's still amazing to me that so many people in Uganda do not have access to power. We provide a decentralised, affordable home system that can completely transform lives. An opportunity to rethink the way that we can achieve universal access to energy," she said.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [2]
>>
